# Line endings.
#
# Default: let git normalise text in the repository to LF and check it out
# per-platform. The exceptions below are files whose ending is functional
# rather than cosmetic.
* text=auto

# cmd.exe is not reliably LF-tolerant -- goto labels and multi-line blocks in
# an LF-only .bat are a known source of "the system cannot find the batch
# label" -- so batch files stay CRLF on every platform.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts and makefiles stay LF even when checked out on Windows;
# a CRLF shebang line is not a shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Relation and factor-base data are a wire format shared with msieve/CADO and
# GGNFS, and the sieve now writes them in binary mode on both platforms.
# Never let git rewrite their endings.
*.fb1 -text
*.afb -text
*.dat -text
